# Transaction Safety & Outbox

Never perform external I/O inside an open database transaction.

## Forbidden

```text
BEGIN → DB write → Twilio / SMS / email / webhook / LiveKit HTTP → COMMIT
```

## Required

```text
BEGIN → business row + outbox pending → COMMIT
→ worker claim → COMMIT claim
→ external I/O
→ UPDATE sent | retry | dead_letter | skipped
```

## Outbox

- Table: `notification_outbox`
- Enqueue only in request handlers (`NotificationService.enqueue_*`)
- Deliver only in `NotificationOutboxWorker` (`python -m callbot_platform.workers.run_outbox`)
- Channels: `sms`, `email`, `webhook`
- Use stable per-tenant `idempotency_key`
- Claim with `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`; never hold locks during provider calls
- Set `TenantContext` from the outbox row’s `tenant_id` in workers (no HTTP session)
- Leases + reclaim on expiry; graceful SIGTERM via worker lifecycle helpers

## Config (do not hard-code)

`OUTBOX_BATCH_SIZE`, `OUTBOX_MAX_RETRIES`, `OUTBOX_BASE_BACKOFF_SECONDS`, `OUTBOX_MAX_BACKOFF_SECONDS`, `OUTBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS`, `OUTBOX_LEASE_SECONDS`

## Provider dual-writes

Purchase / connect / release / dispatch refresh / Stripe signup-checkout use **`async_jobs` sagas** (not inline provider I/O in the request TX). See `.cursor/rules/async-jobs-sagas.mdc` and `docs/SAGA_ARCHITECTURE.md`.

See: `docs/OUTBOX_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/TRANSACTION_AUDIT.md`
